# WHAT: what never enters the Docker build context.
# WHY:  the context is the repo root, so without this every build ships ~74 MB
#       to the daemon — and, more importantly, ships `.env`. Nothing copies it
#       today (the Dockerfile takes only pyproject.toml, control/ and edge/), but
#       the first `COPY . .` anyone writes would bake real secrets into a layer.
#       This is the structural guard behind "never baked into an image layer"
#       in .claude/projects/04-infra-rulebook.md.
# HOW:  deny the risky and the useless; the Dockerfile names what it wants.

.env
# EVERY DEPTH, and the `**` is the whole of the fix — M27.7. A pattern here is matched
# against the WHOLE relative path (Go's filepath.Match, which no `*` crosses a `/` in),
# so the `*.key` and `*.pem` that stood here reached the repository root and nothing
# else. Measured on 2026-09-27 with a build that copied the directory below: the private
# half of the fleet's delivery wildcard — which answers for every delivery name until it
# expires — was in the layer. Nothing ships it today, for the same reason nothing ships
# `.env`: `control.Dockerfile` copies only pyproject.toml, control/ and edge/.
**/*.key
**/*.pem
# And the directory itself, because the guard above is about the extension and this is
# about the contents: `.env.example` tells the operator to put the delivery pair here
# under whatever names their issuer produced, and a `fullchain.crt` is the same key
# material with a name no pattern above matches.
deploy/delivery/
secrets/

.venv/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
docs/
tests/
.e2e/
*_cache/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
